 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Gate drive",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Threshold is 0.65 V minimum, 0.9 V typical and 1.5 V maximum at 250 μA with gate and drain tied. On-resistance is specified at 2.5 A for three gate voltages: 35 mΩ typical and 50 mΩ maximum at 10 V, 38 and 58 mΩ at 4.5 V, 50 and 90 mΩ at 2.5 V. Between 25 °C and 150 °C it rises by a factor of about 1.6 to 1.7. The gate withstands ±12 V; leakage is at most ±100 nA at that voltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Switching",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "With 10 V on the gate, 15 V on the drain, a 3.75 Ω load and a 6.0 Ω gate source resistance, typical delays are 4.0 ns on and 18 ns off, with 2.0 ns rise and fall. Total gate charge is 5.0 nC typical, of which 1.0 nC is gate-source and 2.0 nC gate-drain; the Miller plateau sits near 2 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-drain body diode drops at most 1.0 V carrying 1.0 A with the gate at 0 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Heat",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Dissipation is rated 1.0 W with the ambient at 25 °C, and the steady-state junction-to-ambient thermal resistance is 125 °C/W. The transient thermal impedance curves of Fig. 7 are normalized to RθJA = 100 °C/W. Junction and storage temperatures span -55 °C to +150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Trench MV power MOSFET technology. The SOT-23 mold compound carries a UL 94V-0 flammability rating and is RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and pass the solderability test of MIL-STD-750 method 2026."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Named applications: battery-powered systems, solid-state relays, and direct interfacing to TTL and CMOS logic. A voltage-controlled small-signal switch with fast switching speed."
  }
